tml#p:frame-moment","release_id":"openai-math","schema":"statement-map-web/2","section":3,"section_title":"Integrated moments of orthonormal projections","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:9a259cab8959f233393387e1033c75349c2a8b1a3713611e8aeae56ba1dcad40","file":"preprints/Projection-moments-positive-cap-domination-and-Riesz-estimates-on-the-sphere-September-27-2026/build/sections/projection.tex","line":168,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"966afc2e0aa3a7b81f2ea5113829b9a1a823c750e6d7bff5c5aaaa1d8479cccc","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Projection-moments-positive-cap-domination-and-Riesz-estimates-on-the-sphere-September-27-2026/build/sections/projection.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:9a259cab8959f233393387e1033c75349c2a8b1a3713611e8aeae56ba1dcad40","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Projection-moments-positive-cap-domination-and-Riesz-estimates-on-the-sphere-September-27-2026/build/sections/projection.tex#L168"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{p:frame-moment}\nLet \\(d,k,q\\) be integers and \\(\\beta\\) a real number with\n\\(k\\ge1\\), \\(q\\ge2\\), and\n\\begin{equation}\\label{p:frame-margins}\n k+q\\le d,\\qquad 0<\\beta\\le d,\\qquad\n \\beta-k-(q-2)\\ge1.\n\\end{equation}\nLet \\(\\nu\\) be a finite positive Borel measure supported in\n\\(B(z,R)\\), \\(R>0\\), satisfying \\eqref{p:all-ball-mass} for some\n\\(K\\ge0\\). Assume that \\(P_\\#\\nu\\) is absolutely continuous with\nrespect to Lebesgue measure for \\(\\vartheta_{d,k}\\)-almost every \\(P\\).\nThere is a jointly measurable version \\(g(P,u)\\) of its density such that\n\\begin{equation}\\label{p:frame-moment-bound}\n \\left(\\int_{\\mathcal V_{d,k}}\\int_{\\R^k}g(P,u)^q\\,du\\,\n d\\vartheta_{d,k}(P)\\right)^{1/q}\n \\le C^d(C\\sqrt d)^{k(1-1/q)}\n K R^{\\beta-k(1-1/q)}.\n\\end{equation}\nFor every \\(P\\), this version vanishes when \\(\\norm{u-Pz}>R\\)."}
